===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|ぼら|yomi=k|alt=鰡}}
{{swp|ja:ボラ}}

{{unk|ja}}.  Japanese dictionaries do not indicate when this term first appears in text.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJS">{{R:Daijisen}}</ref><ref name="DJR"/><ref name="SMK5"/>

Monolingual sources speculate that this may be from some element ''ho'' ("[[fat]]") + {{m|ja|腹|tr=hara||[[belly]]}},<ref>[https://gogen-yurai.jp/bora/ Entry at Gogen-Allguide] (in Japanese)</ref><ref>[http://www.nihonjiten.com/data/45708.html Entry at Nihon Jiten] (in Japanese)</ref> but there is no solid evidence for any ''ho'' element with this meaning; the closest by sound is {{m|ja|頬|tr=ho||[[cheek]]|pos=from ancient ''popo''}}, and the closest by meaning is {{m|ja|太|tr=futo||[[fatness]]|pos=from ancient ''puto''}}.

The same fish name has suggestive overlap with {{cog|cop-sah|ⲃⲱⲣⲉ}}, {{cog|cop-boh|ⲫⲟⲣⲓ}} and {{m|cop|ϥⲟⲣⲓ}}, whence its modern {{cog|ar|-}} name {{m|ar|بُورِي}}.

