===Usage notes===
The fish {{taxfmt|Mugil cephalus|species}} is variously called {{lang|ja|ボラ, トド, イナ}} or {{lang|ja|ナヨシ}}. The former term is most general, or sometimes refers specifically to specimens of about 30 to 40 cm in total length.<ref name="DD">{{R:Digital-Daijisen|鯔}}</ref> The term {{lang|ja|イナ}} sometimes refers specifically to young specimens under 20 cm in length,<ref name="DD"/><ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref> as does the archaic {{lang|ja|ナヨシ}}, though {{lang|ja|イナ}} can also refer to the species generally.<ref>'''2001''', プログレッシブ和英中辞典 ''(Progressive Japanese-English Dictionary)'' (in Japanese), Tōkyō: Shogakukan</ref> The form {{lang|ja|トド}} refers to the largest specimens, usually over 50 cm.<ref name="DD" /><ref name="KDJ"/>  Mullet less than 10 cm are sometimes called {{ja-r|スバシリ}} or {{ja-r|オボコ}}.<ref name="DD" />

